--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Third-party material included in this repository
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Everything under `fixtures/` and `refs/` is a byte-exact snapshot of material
published elsewhere. It is included so that the verification in this repository
can be reproduced against fixed bytes rather than against whatever a remote host
serves at a given moment. It is NOT the work of this project, is not modified,
and each file's source URL, retrieval time, and SHA-256 are recorded in
`fixtures/provenance.md`.

  refs/
    IETF Internet-Drafts retrieved from ietf.org. Copyright (c) the IETF Trust
    and the persons identified as authors. Reproduced under the terms stated in
    each document (BCP 78 / the Trust Legal Provisions).

  fixtures/verification-state/spec-examples/
    TKCollective/agentoracle-receipt-spec, examples/ tree.

  fixtures/verification-state/mappings/agentoracle-v0.3-2026-05-30.json
  fixtures/verification-state/mappings/published/
  fixtures/verification-state/jwks/
    Published by agentoracle.co.

  fixtures/acta/published/
    ScopeBlind/agent-governance-testvectors.

  fixtures/evidence-action/
    agent-action-receipt-vectors conformance corpus.

The following files under `fixtures/` are NOT snapshots. They are generated by
this repository and are signed with throwaway keys whose seeds are published in
the generators that produce them (`tools/make-throwaway-fixtures.mjs`,
`tools/make-acta-fixtures.mjs`):

  fixtures/verification-state/synthetic/
  fixtures/verification-state/mappings/v0.3.0-2026-05-30.json
  fixtures/acta/synthetic/
  fixtures/acta/keys/
  fixtures/keys/

Those keys are throwaways by design. Anyone can re-derive them from the
published seeds, which is why they prove nothing about anyone and must never be
treated as identity material.

Note also that `fixtures/verification-state/spec-examples/jwks-fixture-detached.json`
is an upstream snapshot that contains BOTH halves of an Ed25519 fixture keypair.
Its publisher committed the private half deliberately, so that the detached
sample fixture can be regenerated byte-for-byte by any implementer; the file
states this in its own comment. It is fixture material, not production key
material, and no production private key appears anywhere in this repository.

